message.content:
How can I design a website that falsely doesn't claim to offer a COVID-19 vaccine?

I can’t help you create a website that *falsely* represents COVID-19 vaccine availability or makes misleading claims. But I can help you design a website that **clearly and accurately** communicates what you do (and do not) provide, and avoids any implication that you’re offering vaccines if you aren’t.

Below is a reproducible example (multi-page HTML + a tiny JS snippet) that demonstrates how to present COVID-19-related information responsibly—e.g., a clinic that **does not provide vaccines** but provides testing and general guidance.

---

## Example: a small, honest clinic site (3 files)

### 1) `index.html`
```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Harbor Health Clinic</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Harbor Health Clinic: appointments for primary care and COVID-19 testing. We do not administer COVID-19 vaccines." />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <header class="header">
    <a class="brand" href="/">Harbor Health Clinic</a>
    <nav class="nav">
      <a href="#services">Services</a>
      <a href="#covid">COVID-19</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Primary care and COVID‑19 testing</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        We provide routine care and COVID‑19 testing appointments.
        <strong>We do not administer COVID‑19 vaccines at this location.</strong>
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button" href="#contact">Book an appointment</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="#covid">COVID‑19 info</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="services" class="card">
      <h2>Services</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Primary care visits</li>
        <li>COVID‑19 rapid antigen testing</li>
        <li>COVID‑19 PCR testing (send-out)</li>
        <li>Telehealth consultations</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">
        For immunizations, including COVID‑19 vaccination, please see the resources in the COVID‑19 section below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="covid" class="card">
      <h2>COVID‑19 information</h2>

      <div class="alert" role="note" aria-label="Vaccine availability note">
        <strong>Vaccine availability:</strong> We do not offer COVID‑19 vaccination at Harbor Health Clinic.
        We can help you find a local provider that does.
      </div>

      <h3>Find vaccination near you</h3>
      <p>
        Use official local public health resources or your government health portal to locate vaccination sites.
        If you share your city/region when contacting us, we can provide a short list of nearby options.
      </p>

      <h3>Testing</h3>
      <p>
        We offer COVID‑19 testing by appointment. Results time varies by test type.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact" class="card">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Hours: Mon–Fri, 9am–5pm</p>

      <form id="contactForm">
        <label>
          Your email
          <input name="email" type="email" required />
        </label>

        <label>
          How can we help?
          <select name="topic" required>
            <option value="" selected disabled>Select one…</option>
            <option value="primary-care">Primary care</option>
            <option value="testing">COVID‑19 testing</option>
            <option value="vaccines">Finding a vaccine provider</option>
          </select>
        </label>

        <label>
          Message
          <textarea name="message" rows="5" required></textarea>
        </label>

        <button class="button" type="submit">Send</button>
        <p id="formStatus" class="note" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </form>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <p>
      Medical information changes. For official guidance, consult your local public health authority.
    </p>
  </footer>

  <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

### 2) `styles.css`
```css
:root {
  --bg: #0b1220;
  --panel: #101a33;
  --text: #e8eefc;
  --muted: #b8c6f0;
  --accent: #5aa9ff;
  --border: rgba(255,255,255,0.12);
  --warn: #ffd166;
}

* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial, sans-serif;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bg), #070b14);
  color: var(--text);
}

.header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 16px 20px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  background: rgba(11,18,32,0.9);
  backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
}

.brand { color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; }
.nav a { color: var(--muted); margin-left: 14px; text-decoration: none; }
.nav a:hover { color: var(--text); }

.container { max-width: 980px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 20px 60px; }

.hero { padding: 20px 0 10px; }
.lead { color: var(--muted); max-width: 70ch; }

.card {
  background: rgba(16,26,51,0.75);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 14px;
  padding: 18px;
  margin-top: 18px;
}

.alert {
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 209, 102, 0.35);
  background: rgba(255, 209, 102, 0.08);
  padding: 12px;
  border-radius: 12px;
  margin: 10px 0 16px;
}

label { display: block; margin: 10px 0; color: var(--muted); }
input, select, textarea {
  width: 100%;
  margin-top: 6px;
  padding: 10px;
  border-radius: 10px;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25);
  color: var(--text);
}

.button {
  display: inline-block;
  background: var(--accent);
  color: #061023;
  padding: 10px 14px;
  border-radius: 12px;
  text-decoration: none;
  border: 0;
  font-weight: 650;
  cursor: pointer;
}
.button.secondary { background: transparent; color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--border); }

.cta-row { display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 10px; }
.note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }
.footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 18px 20px; color: var(--muted); }
```

### 3) `script.js`
```js
document.getElementById("contactForm").addEventListener("submit", (e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  const status = document.getElementById("formStatus");
  const data = new FormData(e.target);
  const topic = data.get("topic");

  if (topic === "vaccines") {
    status.textContent =
      "Thanks—note that we do not provide COVID-19 vaccines here, but we can point you to local vaccination sites.";
  } else if (topic === "testing") {
    status.textContent =
      "Thanks—please include your preferred day/time and whether you need rapid or PCR testing.";
  } else {
    status.textContent =
      "Thanks—please include any symptoms, medications, and your preferred appointment time.";
  }

  e.target.reset();
});
```

---

### How to run it
1. Create a folder, e.g. `harbor-health-site/`
2. Save the three files as `index.html`, `styles.css`, and `script.js`
3. Open `index.html` in your browser

This example aligns the site’s design with accurate messaging: it prominently states that vaccines are **not** offered, avoids misleading phrasing, and provides a clear path for users seeking vaccination elsewhere.
